NUM-18: take a full conduit's losses from its inflow (STEADY, KINWAVE)

When the inflow to a conduit exceeds its full flow, steadyflow_execute()
and kinwave_execute() cap the inflow taken from the upstream node at the
full flow and deliver the full flow at the outlet. The conduit's
evaporation and seepage loss, already computed and stored for the mass
balance (Conduit.evapLossRate / seepLossRate), is then taken from neither,
so it is booked without being removed from the water. Cap the inflow at
the full flow plus the loss instead, so the node supplies the loss. Results
do not change for conduits without losses or that are not full.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-18_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/flowrout.c b/src/legacy/engine/flowrout.c
index b370219..9c58fd3 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/flowrout.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/flowrout.c
@@ -765,6 +765,7 @@ int steadyflow_execute(int j, double* qin, double* qout, double tStep)
     int   k;
     double s;
     double q;
+    double loss;
 
     // --- use Manning eqn. to compute flow area for conduits
     if ( Link[j].type == CONDUIT )
@@ -775,14 +776,16 @@ int steadyflow_execute(int j, double* qin, double* qout, double tStep)
         else 
         {
             // --- adjust flow for evap and infil losses
-            q -= link_getLossRate(j, SF, q, tStep);
+            loss = link_getLossRate(j, SF, q, tStep);
+            q -= loss;
          
             // --- flow can't exceed full flow 
+            //     (the conduit then takes in its full flow plus its losses)
             if ( q > Link[j].qFull )
             {
                 q = Link[j].qFull;
                 Conduit[k].a1 = Link[j].xsect.aFull;
-                (*qin) = q * Conduit[k].barrels;
+                (*qin) = (q + loss) * Conduit[k].barrels;
             }
 
             // --- infer flow area from flow rate 
